.TH TRANSIP-DNS 1 "October 2026" "transip-rest" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
transip-dns \- manage DNS records at TransIP from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B transip-dns
.RB [ --global-key ]
.RI "{ " \-\-username\~ USER\~ \-\-key\-file\~ KEYFILE " | " \-\-credentials\-ini\~ FILE " }"
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B transip-dns
authenticates to the TransIP API v6 using an RSA key pair and manages
DNS records (A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, NS, TXT, SRV, SSHFP, TLSA, CAA,
NAPTR) for domains in that TransIP account.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI list\~ DOMAIN
List all DNS entries for
.IR DOMAIN .
.TP
.BI add\~ DOMAIN\~NAME\~TYPE\~CONTENT\~ "[\-\-ttl SECONDS]"
Add a DNS entry. Default TTL is 86400 seconds.
.TP
.BI update\~ DOMAIN\~NAME\~TYPE\~CONTENT\~ "[\-\-ttl SECONDS]"
Change an existing entry's content in place via TransIP's PATCH
endpoint, instead of a separate delete then add. The
.IR name ,
.I type
and
.I ttl
must match the live record exactly (TransIP identifies which entry to
update by these three, not by its current content) - only
.I content
changes. Use
.B delete
then
.B add
instead to change a record's ttl or type.
.TP
.BI delete\~ DOMAIN\~NAME\~TYPE\~CONTENT\~ "[\-\-ttl SECONDS]"
Delete a DNS entry. The
.I name
,
.IR type ,
.I content
and
.I ttl
must all match the live record exactly, or TransIP will not find a
match to delete.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --username\~ USER
TransIP account login. Must be combined with
.BR --key-file ,
not with
.BR --credentials-ini .
.TP
.BI --key-file\~ KEYFILE
Path to the RSA private key (PEM) registered for this account. Must
be combined with
.BR --username ,
not with
.BR --credentials-ini .
.TP
.BI --credentials-ini\~ FILE
Path to a credentials file with
.B dns_transip_username
and
.B dns_transip_key_file
keys - the same file format and key names the
.B certbot-dns-transip
plugin's own credentials file uses, so one file can serve both tools.
An alternative to
.B --username
/
.BR --key-file ;
combining this with either of those is an error.
.TP
.B --global-key
Request a token that works from any IP, instead of one limited to
whitelisted IPs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://api.transip.nl/rest/docs.html
TransIP REST API documentation
.UE
